---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { vendors, VERIFIED_LABEL } from '../data/site.js';
---
<Base
  title="Affiliate disclosure — exactly who pays MedSpaStack"
  description="A named list of which med spa software vendors pay us commission and which do not, and how we keep that out of the research."
  crumbs={["Affiliate disclosure"]}
>
<p class="ms-eyebrow">Transparency</p>
<h1 class="ms-display">Affiliate disclosure</h1>

<p class="ms-lede ms-measure">
  MedSpaStack earns affiliate commission from some of the software vendors covered on this site.
  This page names them. Most disclosures in this category are a single sentence in a footer; we
  think you are entitled to the list.
</p>

<div class="ms-callout ms-callout-accent">
  <p class="ms-measure">
    <strong>Current status, {VERIFIED_LABEL}:</strong> MedSpaStack is newly launched and does not
    yet have an active affiliate relationship with any vendor. Applications are in progress. This
    page will be updated with the specific vendors, and the date each relationship began, before
    any paid link appears anywhere on the site.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="ms-h2">The rules we hold ourselves to</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Every vendor is listed here</strong> — paying and non-paying — so you can see the
    shape of the incentive rather than take our word that it does not matter.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Ordering is never by commission.</strong> Tables on this site sort by published price
    or alphabetically. Never by what we earn.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Non-paying vendors get equal coverage.</strong> Several of the most clinically capable
    systems in this category run no affiliate program at all. They are researched and published on
    exactly the same terms, because leaving them out would make the site useless to the buyers who
    need them.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>The research is generated from vendor documentation.</strong> Our pricing database is
    built by reading published pricing pages, not by editorial preference. That is a structural
    safeguard, not a promise.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Commission never buys a mention, a rating, or a removal.</strong> No vendor has, or
    will have, editorial input on this site.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2 class="ms-h2">All platforms we cover</h2>
<p class="ms-measure">
  As relationships begin, the right-hand column will change from "None" to the program name and
  start date.
</p>
<div class="ms-scroller">
<table class="ms-data">
  <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Commercial relationship</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    {vendors.map(v => (
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`/software/${v.slug}/`}>{v.name}</a></td>
        <td>None</td>
      </tr>
    ))}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2 class="ms-h2">Why we are this specific about it</h2>
<p class="ms-measure">
  In med spa software, the most established "independent" comparison resources have real commercial
  ties to platforms they review — in at least one prominent case, the founder holds a senior role at
  a vendor covered on the site. That is disclosed, but it is disclosed in a way most readers will
  never encounter.
</p>
<p class="ms-measure">
  We are not claiming to be purer than anyone. We take affiliate money and we intend to take more
  of it. The difference we are trying to hold is that you should be able to see the whole incentive
  structure on one page, in one table, without having to look anyone up.
</p>

<p class="ms-stamp-note">
  Questions about any of this: hello@medspastack.net ·
  <a href="/methodology/">Full methodology</a>
</p>
</Base>
